    "title": "Full spectral integrality and its converse for power-integral matrices",
    "description": "For a square matrix over a number field K with ring of integers O_K, prove the equivalence of: (i) some positive power of the matrix lies in M_d(O_K); (ii) the characteristic polynomial has all coefficients in O_K; (iii) every eigenvalue is an algebraic integer. The forward directions follow from the fact that a single integral power forces every eigenvalue to be integral (its n-th power is an eigenvalue of the integral power, and algebraic integers are closed under n-th roots). The open converse is (ii) or (iii) implying (i): show that an integral characteristic polynomial forces some power of the matrix to be integral, and bound the smallest such power in terms of denominators appearing in a triangularizing basis.",
    "tags": ["NumberTheory", "LinearAlgebra"]
  },
  {
    "title": "Multiplicativity of the pseudo-determinant on commuting matrices with common kernel",
